Subject: [PATCH] tools/lkl: drop -lgcc for Android hijack/zpoline (use compiler-rt)

LKL's LD_PRELOAD syscall-hijack helper libraries explicitly link against
`-lgcc` on aarch64 (and arm, riscv64) so they have the compiler builtins
they need for things like 64-bit division on 32-bit targets, complex
arithmetic, atomic helpers, etc. The Android NDK does NOT ship libgcc —
modern Android uses clang's compiler-rt builtins instead. The link step
fails with:

  ld.lld: error: unable to find library -lgcc

clang on the NDK target adds compiler-rt builtins automatically when it
acts as the linker driver, even when `-nodefaultlibs` is set, via the
implicit `-rtlib=compiler-rt`. So on Android we simply omit `-lgcc` from
the hijack/zpoline LDLIBS and let clang's default rtlib handle the
builtins; `-lc` is still added so libc gets pulled in for the host stub.

---
 tools/lkl/Targets | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/lkl/Targets b/tools/lkl/Targets
--- a/tools/lkl/Targets
+++ b/tools/lkl/Targets
@@ -8,9 +8,13 @@ libs-$(LKL_HOST_CONFIG_POSIX) += lib/hijack/liblkl-zpoline
 endif
 LDFLAGS_lib/hijack/liblkl-hijack-y += -shared -nodefaultlibs
 LDLIBS_lib/hijack/liblkl-hijack-y += -ldl
+# NDK doesn't ship libgcc; clang's compiler-rt provides the builtins.
+ifneq ($(LKL_HOST_CONFIG_ANDROID),y)
 LDLIBS_lib/hijack/liblkl-hijack-$(LKL_HOST_CONFIG_ARM) += -lgcc -lc
 LDLIBS_lib/hijack/liblkl-hijack-$(LKL_HOST_CONFIG_AARCH64) += -lgcc -lc
 LDLIBS_lib/hijack/liblkl-hijack-$(LKL_HOST_CONFIG_RISCV64) += -lgcc -lc
+endif
+LDLIBS_lib/hijack/liblkl-hijack-$(LKL_HOST_CONFIG_ANDROID) += -lc
 LDLIBS_lib/hijack/liblkl-hijack-$(LKL_HOST_CONFIG_I386) += -lc_nonshared

 LDFLAGS_lib/hijack/liblkl-zpoline-$(LKL_HOST_CONFIG_POSIX) += -shared -nodefaultlibs
